  "text": "Page 4 0f 3/250.081; S0.00°T 50.00 Ciear Creek\nIA'ANANMSААЗИМУНЯ BIII\nregulations stated herein may use the Penalty Assessment Procedure defined under § 16-\n2- 201, C.R.S., as amended, by issuing the violator a penalty assessment notice and\nreleasing the violator upon its terms or, as the law allows, by taking the violator before a\ncounty court judge. The penalty assessment notice shall be a summons and complaint and\nshall contain the identification of the offender, the specification of the offense, and the\napplicable fine.\nSection 8.\nEffective Date.\nThe Board of County Commissioners of Clear Creek County passes this\nOrdinance pursuant to the Colorado General Assembly's mandate under C.R.S. § 30-15-\n401(1)(n.5)(II). Further, the Board of County Commissioners of Clear Creek County\nfinds that this Ordinance is necessary to preserve the public health and safety because of\nthe drought and extreme fire hazard conditions that can exist in the County and the State,\nand, therefore, hereby adopts the Permit System for Open Burning of Slash Piles ir\ninincorporated Clear Creek County as set forth in this Ordinance effective immediatel\nupon signing of this Ordinance.\nFOR PUBLIC HEARING THIS (8/M DAYOF_\nLNLCHEARNG TNSA7 2 DAY OF B/APVEYFOLAND2SDT\nBOARD OF COUNTY\nCOMMISSIONERS\nCLEAR CREEK COUNTY,\nCOLORADO\nRЛA\nRandall Wheelock, Chairman\nGeorge Marlin, Commissioner\nC Wual\nSeamCYood, Commissioner\nATTEST:\nSsнer\nDeputy Clerk and Recorder\nfor Brenda L. Corbett\nClear Creek County Clerk and Recorder\nCERTIFICATION: THE FOREGOING ORDINANCE WAS INTRODUCED AND\nREAD ON April (8y 2023, BY THE BOARD OF COUNTY COMMISSIONERS\nOF CLEAR CREEK COUNTY, COLORADO, AND APPROVED FOR\nPUBLICATION.\nDAIE OF PUBLICATION: April 22, 2023\naatucthel\nE.A. Luther, Deputy Clerk & Recorder\n•\nClear Creek County\n4",
